Package: haploStack
Title: Haplotype Block Analysis and Stacking Simulation for Genomic
        Breeding
Version: 0.8.3
Authors@R: 
    person("Chensong", "Chen",
           email = "chensong.chen@uq.edu.au", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A toolkit for haplotype block definition, catalogue construction,
    and breeding-cycle simulation (haplotype stacking) in diploid crop species.
    The workflow covers four main stages: (1) genotype format standardisation,
    (2) haplotype blocks, from a block map the user supplies (optionally built
    locally from LD with HapSelect or SelectionTools), (3) haplotype
    catalogue construction — per-sample local GEBVs, Manhattan plots, and
    alignment visualisations — and (4) crossing-design simulation using Genetic
    Algorithm (GA), Genomic Selection (GS), and Optimal Contribution Selection
    (OCS) strategies. Designed for the GRDC barley haplotype stacking project
    but applicable to any biparental or multiparental breeding programme.
